# Trading settings kept in git, so a push to master changes them. Loaded after
# /etc/tempest/bot.env (docker-compose.yml), so these win over the same keys
# there. Secrets and the owner's other risk settings (LEVERAGE,
# DAILY_DRAWDOWN_PCT) stay in bot.env on the server. Never put a key here:
# this repo is public.
#
# 2026-11-07 (owner): the lab's only setup that held up out of sample,
# breakout on 1d trend / 4h signal; three liquid pairs; at most three
# positions, each with a third of the margin.
# 2026-11-10 (owner): fewer, larger positions: at most two, half the margin
# each. One slot at 20x would put liquidation (~5 %) inside the usual 4h stop
# (6-8 %), so most entries would be refused.
# 2026-11-13 (owner): the same ten pairs the nightly lab measures, so live
# trades what the numbers come from. Still at most two positions.
TRADING_PAIRS=BTCUSDC,ETHUSDC,SOLUSDC,BNBUSDC,XRPUSDC,DOGEUSDC,ADAUSDC,LINKUSDC,AVAXUSDC,LTCUSDC
MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS=2
TREND_INTERVAL=1d
SIGNAL_INTERVAL=4h
# 2026-11-10 (owner): once a position is up 100 % on its margin (5 % at
# 20x), its stop moves to the entry price. Lab, 2 years, same 5 % move:
# profit factor 1.35 -> 1.44 out of sample on ten pairs, 1.82 -> 1.66 on
# BTC/ETH/SOL; lower drawdowns in three of four runs.
BREAKEVEN_ROI_PCT=100
# 2026-11-14 (owner: "do what you think is best", after the account passed 250):
# 15 % of equity at the stop per trade, down from 80 % (which the margin cap
# held at ~58 %). Two stops together cost ~30 %, not the whole account. A simple
# model (37 % hits, 2R targets) gives ~48 % to reach 1000 from 253 at 15 %,
# against ~25 % at the old size. Applies to new positions only.
RISK_PER_TRADE_PCT=15
